   "subject": "Is there an elegant way to set the working directory without providing the whole path each time?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Hi</font><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I know that in order to set the working directory you need to provide the whole path by setwd(&quot;C:/Users/Ayala/Documents&quot;). Is there a more elegant way to do that such that you won&#39;t need to provide the whole path (and also switch the \\ to /) each time?</font></div><div><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">I&#39;m doing the Coursera <span style=\"white-space:nowrap\">R Programming Course and I need to write a function for which one of the arguments is the </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);line-height:21px\">directory and as I said I want to set the directory in a more elegant way. </span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\"><span style=\"line-height:21px;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">When searching the help I cane across the </span></font><a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/normalizePath\" style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128);font-size:medium;font-family:monospace;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/normalizePath&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497938825000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3Izg1cPGk05Q3mGl9O7i2U\">normalizePath</a> and the <a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/shortPathName\" style=\"color:rgb(128,0,128);font-size:medium;font-family:monospace;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/shortPathName&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497938825000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0CIb4cU5lMpIWiHaN3Yhxj\">shortPathName</a> but I&#39;m not sure that is the way to go.<span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);line-height:21px\"><font size=\"2\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></div><div><br></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" size=\"2\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><span style=\"line-height:21px\">I will greatly appreciate a general guidance and not a specific answer because I want to try and figure things on my own.</span></font><span style=\"line-height:21px;font-family:&#39;Helvetica Neue&#39;,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">  </span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:21px\">Best,</span></font></div><div><font color=\"#333333\" face=\"Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif\" size=\"2\"><span style=\"line-height:21px\">Ayala</span></font></div><h3 style=\"color:rgb(102,102,102);font-family:monospace;font-size:large;line-height:normal;background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><br></h3><div>  </div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "sZugh1AJI7YJ",
