   "subject": "RE: [Israel RUG] Is there an elegant way to set the working directory without providing the whole path each time?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hi,<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">The function getwd() returns the absolute path of your working directory.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">So you can use it to get you initial path and the paste to it the rest of the path.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">For example:<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"># Set Working Diretory<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">mywd &lt;- &quot;</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> C:/Users/Ayala/Documents</span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"> &quot;<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"># Source code directory<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">setwd(mywd)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"># R code directory<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">R_code_dir &lt;- paste (mywd, &quot;\\\\R-scripts\\\\&quot;,sep=&quot;&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Ofrit<u></u><u></u></span></p></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div lang=\"EN-US\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\"><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a> [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a>] <b>On Behalf Of </b>Ayala Allon<br><b>Sent:</b> Friday, 20 June 2014 10:16 AM<br><b>To:</b> <a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">israel-r-...@googlegroups.com</a><br><b>Subject:</b> [Israel RUG] Is there an elegant way to set the working directory without providing the whole path each time?<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Hi</span><u></u><u></u></p><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I know that in order to set the working directory you need to provide the whole path by setwd(&quot;C:/Users/Ayala/Documents&quot;). Is there a more elegant way to do that such that you won&#39;t need to provide the whole path (and also switch the \\ to /) each time?</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">I&#39;m doing the Coursera R Programming Course and I need to write a function for which one of the arguments is the <span style=\"color:#333333\">directory and as I said I want to set the directory in a more elegant way. </span></span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#333333\">When searching the help I cane across the </span><a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/normalizePath\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/normalizePath&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497938828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3cJY1er3G7pEOipUWwLrZB\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:purple\">normalizePath</span></a> and the <a href=\"http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/shortPathName\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://127.0.0.1:31839/library/base/help/shortPathName&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792497938828000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Zf-DWc15P__hgfdt0PXj7\"><span style=\"font-size:13.5pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:purple\">shortPathName</span></a> but I&#39;m not sure that is the way to go.<u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Arial&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#333333\">I will greatly appreciate a general guidance and not a specific answer because I want to try and figure things on my own.</span><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#333333\">  </span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#333333\">Best,</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Helvetica&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#333333\">Ayala</span><u></u><u></u></p></div><h3 style=\"background-image:initial;background-size:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial;background-position:initial;background-repeat:initial\"><span style=\"font-size:18.0pt;font-family:&quot;Courier New&quot;;color:#666666\"><u></u> <u></u></span></h3><div><p class=\"MsoNormal\">  <u></u><u></u></p></div></div></div></div>"
